{
"dur": 41.838,
"shots": [
{
"i": 1,
"start": 0.0,
"vo_start": 0.6,
"vo_end": 6.48,
"text": "Then came the Great Depression in 1929. By early 1933 about six million Germans were out of work.",
"end": 6.755
},
{
"i": 2,
"start": 6.755,
"vo_start": 7.03,
"vo_end": 13.71,
"text": "In January 1933 Hitler became chancellor. Within months he had banned other parties and made himself a dictator.",
"end": 13.985
},
{
"i": 3,
"start": 13.985,
"vo_start": 14.26,
"vo_end": 19.317,
"text": "His plan was an empire for a so-called master race, with 'living space' taken from the east.",
"end": 19.592
},
{
"i": 4,
"start": 19.592,
"vo_start": 19.867,
"vo_end": 28.366,
"text": "In 1935 he revealed an air force and brought back conscription, breaking the treaty. Britain even signed a deal letting Germany build a navy.",
"end": 28.641
},
{
"i": 5,
"start": 28.641,
"vo_start": 28.916,
"vo_end": 35.276,
"text": "In 1936 his troops marched into the Rhineland, next to France. France and Britain did nothing.",
"end": 35.551
},
{
"i": 6,
"start": 35.551,
"vo_start": 35.826,
"vo_end": 40.888,
"text": "France was already relying on the Maginot Line, a huge chain of forts along its border with Germany.",
"end": 41.838
}
],
